25:["$","p","p-7",{"children":"A worker claims a message, reads the current operation, performs or confirms the effect, durably records the result, then acknowledges the message. Acknowledging first can lose work if the worker crashes before recording the result. Acknowledging last can lead to redelivery if the acknowledgement is lost, which is why the effect must tolerate duplicates."}]
26:["$","p","p-8",{"children":"For SQS, a received message becomes temporarily invisible. If processing does not finish and delete the message within that visibility timeout, it can reappear; standard queues may also deliver more than once during the timeout. Other brokers use leases or acknowledgement mechanisms with their own details. Match the lease to expected work, extend it when supported, and still design for overlap."}]
